error[L0510]: cannot return a borrow of a local value
  --> check/closure_capturing_lends_local_borrow.rslisp:10:50
   |
10 |   (let owned-year (fn ((c car)) (println offset) (ref (:year c))))
   |                        -------                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this borrows a local value
   |                        |
   |                        this parameter owns its value, which is dropped when the function returns
   |
   = help: return an owned value with `(clone ...)`, or capture the value instead of passing it

error[L0512]: cannot pass a borrow of a local value to `first`
  --> check/closure_capturing_lends_local_borrow.rslisp:15:19
   |
 4 |   (let years (vec 2019 2021 2024))
   |        ----- this local is dropped when the function returns
...
 7 |   (let first (fn ((items (ref (vec i64)))) (println offset) (at items 0)))
   |                   ----------------------- `first` ties this parameter to its result, so it needs a borrow that outlives the function
...
15 |   (println (first (ref years)))
   |                   ^^^^^^^^^^^ this borrows a local value
   |
   = help: define `first` with `defn`, where its result can borrow from its argument

